# Manifest of source vendored from upstream Kubernetes COSI.
#
# hack/resync.sh reads this file. Any file added to or removed from the vendored
# set must be recorded here, or it silently stops being checked against upstream.
#
# Every listed file is byte-identical to upstream except for its import block,
# which is rewritten from upstream's internal/ layout to Trident package paths
# and reordered to satisfy goimports. resync.sh compares file bodies with the
# import block removed, so those rewrites are expected and ignored.
#
# A line ending in "diverged" marks a file we edit on purpose. Every such edit is
# logged at the bottom of this file and tagged "NETAPP LOCAL" in the source, so a
# re-sync is a review of a known list rather than archaeology. Keep the list
# short: each entry is a merge conflict waiting for the next pin bump.
#
# One commit governs three things and they must never drift apart:
#   1. the files listed below
#   2. the client and proto module pseudo-versions in go.mod
#   3. the CRD YAML Trident installs
# There is no upstream tag to anchor to: the only published tag of client/proto
# contains v1alpha1 only, and v1alpha2 exists solely on untagged main.

repo   kubernetes-sigs/container-object-storage-interface
commit e761fd730bf4617dd42c9e585626ee95e88a8b62

